Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-lock
Architecture: all
# python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the lock screen (GTK 3, the
# Arc theme; gi-cairo for drawing the wallpaper and the picture).
# gir1.2-gtksessionlock-0.1: ext-session-lock-v1 from GTK, so a crash keeps
# the screens covered (19 KB). libgtk-session-lock0 (274 KB): the library it
# describes, which trixie's gir package doesn't depend on (without it the lock
# screen can't start and swaylock takes over every time).
# libpam0g: the password check (through ctypes, no Python module).
# swaylock: takes over whenever the lock screen can't (ADR-003, ADR-004).
# flickos-control 1.48 runs it (Super+L, the menus, swayidle); an older one
# would leave it unused, so installing it brings the newer one along.
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gtksessionlock-0.1,
         libgtk-session-lock0,
         libpam0g,
         swaylock,
         ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: flickos-control (<< 1.48~)
Description: lock screen of the FlickOS desktop
 Locks the screen with a password box that can show the password, the time,
 the date and the user's name and picture, in the colors of the desktop style
 in use.
 .
 The screen is covered at once, before the lock screen itself has loaded,
 and stays covered if the lock screen stops working: swaylock then takes
 over. FlickOS's Settings run it for Super+L, the menus and the idle lock.
